{
  "schema_version": "report-evidence/1",
  "source_sha256": "8960e678842e7db6482a6b429175bbc634e38292bd453c5958c32e0065c566dc",
  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0001",
      "text": "External Balance Check in WERC7575ShareToken::unregisterVault Enables Vault Registry Denial-of-Service",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 102,
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0002",
      "text": "## Summary",
      "start": 104,
      "end": 114,
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0003",
      "text": "The `unregisterVault()` function in `WERC7575ShareToken` can be permanently blocked by sending 1 wei of the underlying asset directly to the vault address. Combined with the `MAX_VAULTS_PER_SHARE_TOKEN = 10` limit, this allows an attacker to fill all registry slots and then \"dust\" each vault, permanently locking the vault registry.",
      "start": 115,
      "end": 448,
      "line": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0004",
      "text": "## Vulnerability Details",
      "start": 450,
      "end": 474,
      "line": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0005",
      "text": "### Root Cause",
      "start": 476,
      "end": 490,
      "line": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0006",
      "text": "The `unregisterVault()` function enforces a strict balance check:",
      "start": 491,
      "end": 556,
      "line": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0007",
      "text": "This check uses `balanceOf()` (external balance) rather than internal accounting (`totalAssets()`). Neither `WERC7575Vault` nor `ERC7575VaultUpgradeable` implements a `sweep()` function to remove excess tokens not backed by shares.",
      "start": 559,
      "end": 790,
      "line": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0008",
      "text": "### Attack Vector",
      "start": 792,
      "end": 809,
      "line": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0009",
      "text": "1. Attacker sends 1 wei of the underlying asset directly to the vault contract address",
      "start": 811,
      "end": 897,
      "line": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0010",
      "text": "2. Admin attempts to call `unregisterVault()`",
      "start": 898,
      "end": 943,
      "line": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0011",
      "text": "3. Transaction reverts with `CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance()` because `balanceOf(vault) == 1`",
      "start": 944,
      "end": 1041,
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0012",
      "text": "4. Vault remains registered indefinitely",
      "start": 1042,
      "end": 1082,
      "line": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0013",
      "text": "### Registry Lockout Scenario",
      "start": 1084,
      "end": 1113,
      "line": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0014",
      "text": "## Recommended Mitigations",
      "start": 1116,
      "end": 1142,
      "line": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0015",
      "text": "Replace `balanceOf()` with `totalAssets()` which tracks internal accounting:",
      "start": 1143,
      "end": 1219,
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "e_8960e678842e_0016",
      "text": "or you can add a function to remove dust from vaults:",
      "start": 1222,
      "end": 1275,
      "line": 28
    }
  ]
}
